{:name "Interest accrual + capitalisation on a customer savings account"
 :tags #{:edn-only :interest :savings}
 ;; Tenant onboards a person-party, defines and publishes a savings
 ;; product with a non-zero interest rate, opens a customer savings
 ;; account, funds it from settlement, then runs accrue and capitalise.
 ;; Both steps post real transactions:
 ;;
 ;;   accrual     credits customer.interest-accrued, and writes no
 ;;               transaction at all. The bank's side is one entry
 ;;               for the run: DR 5100 expense / CR 2400 payable.
 ;;
 ;;   capitalise  debits  customer.interest-accrued \  the statement
 ;;               credits customer.default          /  line, 2 legs
 ;;               and one entry per currency and product type at
 ;;               close: DR 2400 payable / CR the deposit control.
 ;;
 ;; The customer's *available* balance — what `project-balances`
 ;; reads — covers `default` + `default-pending-*` only, so neither
 ;; accrual nor capitalisation visibly moves it. Locking in the
 ;; cross-balance-type effects needs richer projections (see plan
 ;; task 6.x); this scenario checks the wiring runs without an
 ;; anomaly.
 :given [{:command :create-bank :args []}                         ; org-0,
                                                                  ; prod-0
                                                                  ; (settlement),
                                                                  ; party-0
                                                                  ; (org),
                                                                  ; acct-0
         {:command :create-product :args [:bank-0 :savings 3650]} ; prod-1
                                                                  ; (savings,
                                                                  ; draft,
                                                                  ; 36.5% AER)
         {:command :publish-product :args [:prod-1]} ; prod-1 published
         {:command :create-person-party :args [:bank-0]}           ; party-1
                                                                   ; (person,
                                                                   ; auto-active)
         {:command :open-account :args [:bank-0 :party-1 :prod-1]} ; acct-1
                                                                   ; (savings,
                                                                   ; customer)
         {:command :inbound-transfer :args [:acct-0 100000]}           ; £1,000
                                                                       ; into
                                                                       ; settlement
         {:command :internal-transfer :args [:acct-0 :acct-1 100000]}] ; settlement
                                                                       ; →
                                                                       ; savings
 ;; The reconciliation runs between the two passes and again after
 ;; capitalisation: what every customer has accrued is what 2400 says
 ;; the bank owes, whatever the run produced. The four pinned
 ;; `:assert-gl-balance` steps below stay — they check the arithmetic,
 ;; this checks the routing.
 :when [{:command :accrue-interest :args [:bank-0 20260501]}
        {:command :assert-interest-reconciliation :args [:bank-0 "GBP"]}
        {:command :capitalize-interest :args [:bank-0 20260501]}
        {:command :assert-interest-reconciliation :args [:bank-0 "GBP"]}]
 ;; Both passes enumerate each customer account into an
 ;; InterestAccountRun row and flip it to done in the same transaction
 ;; as the posting. Scope is 2: acct-1 (savings) and acct-0, which
 ;; `:create-bank` opens on a customer-current product — the bank's 7
 ;; real GL accounts carry no product type and stay out of scope. A row
 ;; reaching done records that an account was considered, whether or
 ;; not it earned anything, which is the only trace a zero-rate account
 ;; leaves. Closed means nothing was left pending.
 ;;
 ;; Accrual writes no per-account transaction — only the customer's
 ;; accrued bucket and the carry. The bank's side is one ledger entry
 ;; for the run, DR 5100 / CR 2400, for what every account earned
 ;; between them. The GL assertions are what prove the books still
 ;; balance, and 100 exercises the case worth proving: acct-1 earns
 ;; 100 on £1,000 at 36.5% AER while acct-0 earns nothing, and
 ;; protojure drops a zero from the wire, so the zero row carries no
 ;; amount at all. A run total of 100 means an absent value
 ;; contributes nothing rather than breaking the aggregate index.
 ;;
 ;; Capitalisation then sweeps the same 100 out of the accrued bucket,
 ;; clearing 2400 back to zero while 5100 keeps the expense. It keeps
 ;; its per-account transaction — that one is the customer's statement
 ;; line — but drops its control legs, so its ledger side is also one
 ;; entry per group: DR 2400 / CR the deposit control the product type
 ;; rolls into. acct-1 is savings, so the 100 lands in 2200 on top of
 ;; the £1,000 already there, and 2100 keeps only acct-0's nil balance.
 ;; Asserting both controls is what proves the aggregate credits the
 ;; right one — a single per-currency entry could not, which is why the
 ;; group is (currency, product type).
 :then [{:command :assert-no-anomaly :args []}
        {:command :assert-interest-run
         :args [:bank-0 20260501 :accrue
                {:scope 2 :done 2 :failed 0 :pending 0
                 :run-state :interest-run-state-closed}]}
        {:command :assert-interest-run
         :args [:bank-0 20260501 :capitalize
                {:scope 2 :done 2 :failed 0 :pending 0
                 :run-state :interest-run-state-closed}]}
        {:command :assert-gl-balance
         :args [:bank-0 :gl-account-code-interest-expense "GBP" -100]}
        {:command :assert-gl-balance
         :args [:bank-0 :gl-account-code-interest-payable "GBP" 0]}
        {:command :assert-gl-balance
         :args [:bank-0 :gl-account-code-customer-deposits-savings
                "GBP" 100100]}
        {:command :assert-gl-balance
         :args [:bank-0 :gl-account-code-customer-deposits-current "GBP" 0]}]}
